          "end": 342
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "[P2] Restore state when metadata arrives after cached data",
      "body": "When a card initially hydrates data from `widgetState` and its snapshot capability arrives later in a metadata-only `openai:set_globals` update, `hasData.current` is already true and this condition skips restoration. The cached result remains visible, but its saved pagination/disclosure state is lost and the first interaction can overwrite it; trigger an `allowDataPresent` restore when a new capability arrives without `toolOutput`.",
